{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2198-05-13 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Patel. I’ll be taking care of you during your stay. You’re here because of nausea and vomiting. Can you tell me what happened?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2198-05-13 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I woke up this morning and just started vomiting. I couldn’t stop. I’ve been having these episodes more often lately."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2198-05-13 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You have Type 1 diabetes and gastroparesis, correct? And a gastric pacemaker?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2198-05-13 14:02:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve had the pacemaker for a few years. It helps a little, but not like it used to."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2198-05-13 14:03:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood sugar was high when you arrived—306—and your anion gap was elevated, which means mild ketoacidosis. That’s likely from not keeping food or insulin down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2198-05-13 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh. I did take my Lantus last night and a little Humalog this morning, but I couldn’t keep anything down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2198-05-13 14:04:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We gave you some insulin and fluids in the ER. You’re on IV fluids now to rehydrate and we’ll keep an eye on your sugars."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2198-05-13 14:05:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been so dehydrated. My mouth feels dry, and I’m dizzy when I sit up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2198-05-13 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. Vomiting a lot can cause volume depletion. Your heart rate is high—139—which is likely from that and the mild DKA."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2198-05-13 14:06:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2198-05-13 14:07:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s concerning, but not critical. We’re treating it with fluids and your usual metoprolol. We switched it to IV for now since you can’t take pills."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2198-05-13 14:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. My blood pressure has been up and down too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2198-05-13 14:08:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we saw that. You were hypertensive in the ER, but it’s improved. We gave IV enalaprilat earlier and will switch back to your lisinopril when you can eat."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2198-05-13 14:09:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I don’t want my blood pressure spiking again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2198-05-13 14:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll monitor it closely. For your nausea, we’re giving IV Zofran and Reglan, and your scopolamine patch is on."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2198-05-13 14:10:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. That patch helps a little. I’ve had Botox injections before for my gastroparesis—those helped too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2198-05-13 14:11:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good to know. We’ll plan for you to follow up with GI soon. They may repeat the Botox if it worked before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2198-05-13 14:12:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’d like that. I’ve been admitted so many times for this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2198-05-13 14:13:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see you were in the hospital last week for DKA. It sounds like your gastroparesis is getting harder to control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2198-05-13 14:13:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, exactly. I can’t keep insulin down, so my sugars go high, and then I get sicker."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2198-05-13 14:14:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re giving you insulin through shots now. Your anion gap has already improved from 20 to 10, which is good progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2198-05-13 14:15:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s reassuring. What about my diet?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2198-05-13 14:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll start you on clear liquids tomorrow if your nausea improves. We’re also treating your GERD with IV omeprazole for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2198-05-13 14:16:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’ve been off my esomeprazole because I wasn’t taking pills."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2198-05-13 14:17:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll restart it by mouth when you can swallow. One more thing—we did a chest X-ray to check your port and make sure there’s no blockage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2198-05-13 14:18:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And? Is everything okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2198-05-13 14:18:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Your port is fine, lungs are clear, and your gastric stimulator is in place. No free air, so no perforation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2198-05-13 14:19:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. That’s a relief."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2198-05-14 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your nausea is better today, I hear. You kept down some apple juice?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2198-05-14 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes! First thing in days. I still feel queasy, but not vomiting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2198-05-14 09:01:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. Your blood sugar is stable—around 150. We switched your IV fluids to D5NS since your sugars came down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2198-05-14 09:02:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What’s D5NS?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2198-05-14 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s saline with dextrose—sugar—to prevent your levels from dropping too low now that you’re not as dehydrated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2198-05-14 09:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Ah, got it. And my insulin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2198-05-14 09:04:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re back on your home Lantus—28 units at night—and Humalog on a sliding scale. We’re watching your response."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2198-05-14 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’m glad we’re getting back to normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2198-05-14 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Quick update—we got your urine culture back. It showed some bacteria, including Group B Strep. Even though you don’t have urinary symptoms, we’re starting ciprofloxacin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2198-05-14 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t know I had a UTI. Should I be worried?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2198-05-14 10:31:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not at all. With diabetes, we treat even asymptomatic infections to prevent complications. It’s just a 4-day course."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2198-05-14 10:32:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. Thank you for explaining."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2198-05-15 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—you’re being discharged today. You had one episode of vomiting this morning when your sugar was high, but you tolerated lunch well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2198-05-15 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Really? That’s great. I feel so much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2198-05-15 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Your anion gap is normal, heart rate is down to 88, and you’re eating. We’re sending you home with your usual meds plus cipro for 4 more days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2198-05-15 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my follow-up with GI?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2198-05-15 08:03:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "In four days. They’ll discuss repeating the Botox injection. Keep using your anti-nausea meds as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2198-05-15 08:04:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you so much for helping me through this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2198-05-15 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Call us if vomiting returns or your sugars go above 300. Otherwise, see you at your follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2198-05-15 08:05:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I’m just glad to be going home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2198-05-15 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final check before discharge: you’re alert, walking fine, and your vitals are stable. All set to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2198-05-15 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I really appreciate everything."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2198-05-13 13:38:00",
    "admission_end": "2198-05-15 16:24:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 30-year-old woman with Type 1 diabetes and gastroparesis was admitted for acute nausea and vomiting leading to mild diabetic ketoacidosis and volume depletion. She was treated with IV fluids, insulin therapy, and antiemetics. Her condition improved over two days, with stabilization of her blood glucose and anion gap, and she advanced to oral intake. A urine culture revealed asymptomatic bacteriuria with Group B Streptococcus, prompting a short course of ciprofloxacin. She was discharged home in stable condition with plans to follow up with gastroenterology for possible Botox injection for gastroparesis.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with ketoacidosis, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Volume depletion, unspecified",
      "Tachycardia, unspecified",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Esophageal reflux"
    ]
  }
}
